From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:57:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] phy: allwinner: Add a driver for the A733 USB3 combo PHY

The first combo PHY in the SERDES block of the A733 is a Cadence PHY in
an Allwinner wrapper and carries the SuperSpeed lanes of the USB3
controller to the Type-C connector.

Add a driver for its USB3 function. It programs the PMA for USB3, routes
the PIPE interface of the controller to this PHY and releases it from
reset with the power state request the controller expects.

If the PHY does not acknowledge the PIPE clock and power state, or its
common PMA block does not become ready, init fails with -ETIMEDOUT and
the clocks and the PHY are taken back, as the controller cannot leave its
core soft reset without the PIPE clock.

The PLL restart follows the vendor code. It and the delays are not
measured on our boards.

The lanes of a flipped plug are swapped inside the PHY, so the driver
registers a Type-C orientation switch. The direction may only change
while the PHY is held in reset, so a new direction on a PHY in use puts
it back into reset, reprograms the lane settings and releases it again.

The PIPE muxes and the lane width conversion sit in the SERDES top page,
shared with the second combo PHY. The driver reaches it through the
syscon regmap and changes only its own fields there, under the regmap
lock.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards without a handshake
timeout; the PHY programs its share of the SERDES top page through the
syscon, and a stick enumerates at SuperSpeed Plus in both plug
directions and reads back the same data; the timeout paths were not
triggered. The driver offers no bind or unbind file in sysfs.

Assisted-by: LLM
